\end{aligned}],v=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]$ and $w=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]$ be vectors such that $v$ and $w$ are orthogonal. Find $(u+9v)\\cdot w+v\\cdot (u+7w).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134208 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ae358486-c985-5c1a-bc7b-7505ecc708f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134208 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $v$ and $w$ are orthogonal vectors, we have that $v\\cdot w=0.$ Therefore, using linearity of the dot product to expand the parentheses, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(u+9v)\\cdot w+v\\cdot (u+7w) & =u\\cdot w+(9v)\\cdot w+v\\cdot u+v\\cdot (7w) \\\\  & =u\\cdot w+9(v\\cdot w)+v\\cdot u+7(v\\cdot w) \\\\  & =u\\cdot w+9\\cdot 0+v\\cdot u+7\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =u\\cdot w+v\\cdot u \\\\  & =(4\\cdot 2+(-2)\\cdot (-5)+1\\cdot 7+(-3)\\cdot (-3)) \\\\  & +((-4)\\cdot 4+3\\cdot (-2)+5\\cdot 1+4\\cdot (-3)) \\\\  & =(8+10+7+9)+(-16-6+5-12) \\\\  & =34-29 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134644 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186134719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134644 #edb/ref 1061 20202 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134644 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "33af035b-34c4-553f-a53d-8f63666f0e02" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134644 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186135037 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134645 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186134646 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134645 #edb/ref 1061 20203 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134645 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "645df347-5e9c-54a1-993b-ebe8a9afb3af" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134645 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186133770 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134646 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186134647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134646 #edb/ref 1061 20204 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134646 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "45beb215-0e09-5673-a4ed-c8979e0e7025" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134646 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186133771 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186134647 #edb/ref 1061 20205 #edb/ref 17